To enforce a color filter in your store, you can use a combination of CSS and JavaScript. Here's a step-by-step guide on how to do it:

1. Set up the HTML structure:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>My Store</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="store-container">
      <div id="filter-container">
        <div class="filter">
          <h2>Filter by Color</h2>
          <input type="color" id="color-input" placeholder="Enter Color">
        </div>
        <div id="color-list"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
```

2. Add the CSS for styling the filter container:

```css
#filter-container {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  padding: 20px;
  background-color: #f2f2f2;
  border-radius: 5px;
}

#color-input {
  width: 100%;
  height: 40px;
  border-radius: 5px;
  background-color: #333;
  color: #ffffff;
  padding: 10px;
}
```

3. Add JavaScript to handle the color selection:

```javascript
function filterColor() {
  // Get the value of the color input
  var colorInput = document.getElementById('color-input');
  var selectedColor = colorInput.value;

  // Add a class to the filter container
  var filterContainer = document.getElementById('filter-container');
  filterContainer.classList.add('filter');

  // Create a new element with the selected color
  var colorElement = document.createElement('div');
  colorElement.classList.add('color-element');
  colorElement.innerHTML = 'Color: ' + selectedColor;

  // Append the colorElement to the filterContainer
  filterContainer.appendChild(colorElement);

  // Set the selected color as the filter
  colorInput.value = selectedColor;
}

